        "original_id": "05ffec55-5db4-54a3-bd0a-82f041879596",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hanns Alexander, Rudolf Höss\n- Roles: German Jewish refugee, SS-Obersturmbannführer, commandant of Auschwitz\n- Places: Auschwitz\n- Events: World War II, arrest of Rudolf Höss\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Höss was born on 25 November 1901 and died on 16 April 1947.\n- Hanns Alexander was born on 6 May 1917 and died on 23 December 2006.\n- Rudolf Höss was a Nazi German SS-Obersturmbannführer, equivalent to lieutenant colonel.\n- During World War II, Rudolf Höss was the longest-serving commandant of Auschwitz concentration and extermination camp.\n- Hanns Alexander was a German Jewish refugee who tracked down and arrested Rudolf Höss, the commandant of Auschwitz.",
